$DIR/main.p:5:32: cannot make a literal of owner type sys.File outside package sys: field fd is unexported
    An owner owns memory or another resource and releases it when it is dropped,
    so it moves instead of being copied. A literal of sys.File makes a new
    owner. sys.File has the unexported field fd, so its package keeps invariants
    that a literal written elsewhere could break, and only that package may make
    one.
    Use a constructor from the package that declares sys.File.
    (see "Conversions" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.24)
    (run "pluto explain E3212" for a longer explanation)

